---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConsultForm from '../components/ConsultForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CFO Market Intelligence for Enterprise AI Investment | Lozen Advisory" description="Independent CFO-focused intelligence on enterprise AI ROI, infrastructure spend, hidden implementation costs, workforce capacity, accountability, and board-level investment risk.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/#services">Services</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; CFO Market Intelligence</div>
    <span class="pill">Independent CFO Intelligence</span>
    <div class="ic-lg"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:52px;height:52px;color:var(--accent-2)"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div>
    <h1>CFO Market Intelligence</h1>
    <p class="sub">Independent analysis for CFOs evaluating whether enterprise AI investment is producing measurable returns or transferring costs into hidden implementation, verification, workforce, and accountability work.</p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a href="#consult" class="btn btn-accent">Request CFO Intelligence →</a>
      <a href="#how" class="btn btn-ghost">How it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2 class="h2">The CFO problem is not a lack of AI information. It is a lack of decision-grade evidence.</h2>
      <p>CFOs are being asked to justify AI spending, evaluate infrastructure costs, measure payback, explain labor assumptions, and present the investment case to boards while deployment is moving faster than the financial record.</p>
      <p>Lozen Advisory separates measurable enterprise value from adoption volume, vendor claims, and incomplete productivity reporting, then translates the findings into the questions finance leadership must resolve before approving, expanding, defending, or restructuring the investment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="checklist" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Enterprise AI ROI and payback analysis</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>AI infrastructure and implementation-cost scrutiny</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Labor ROI, redeployment, and headcount assumptions</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Hidden verification, correction, and exception-handling work</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>Auditability, attribution, and operating-record gaps</p></div>
        <div class="check"><span class="ck">✓</span><p>CFO and board investment implications</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What the intelligence resolves</span>
      <h2 class="h2">From AI investment claim to finance decision</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>ROI scrutiny</h3><p>Test whether the business case measures realized financial value or relies on adoption, output volume, time saved, projected labor reduction, or vendor estimates.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg></div><h3>Total-cost exposure</h3><p>Identify infrastructure, integration, data, licensing, control, training, and ongoing operating costs that determine the real payback period.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg></div><h3>Financial evidence</h3><p>Determine whether finance can connect the claimed return to documented operating results, assumptions, approvals, and accountable owners.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></div><h3>Investment risk</h3><p>Surface financial, operational, auditability, insurance, disclosure, or accountability exposure that the reported return does not capture.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Labor and capacity</h3><p>Test whether AI is eliminating work or relocating it into review, correction, escalation, integration, and accountability carried by existing employees.</p></div>
      <div class="fcard reveal"><div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg></div><h3>Independent intelligence</h3><p>Provide a concise CFO briefing that is not tied to a software sale, implementation mandate, or vendor adoption agenda.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A clear advisory process</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Frame</h3><p>Define the AI ROI, infrastructure, labor, payback, or board-level investment question the CFO needs answered.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Investigate</h3><p>Examine the business case, current market evidence, cost logic, workforce assumptions, operating dependencies, and enterprise exposure.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Translate</h3><p>Convert fragmented AI claims into financial, implementation, workforce, control, accountability, and governance implications.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Brief</h3><p>Deliver a focused CFO intelligence product with evidence gaps, decision questions, exposure signals, and an executive discussion.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>How should a CFO evaluate enterprise AI ROI?</h4><p>The analysis distinguishes adoption and output activity from measurable financial return. It tests the full cost of infrastructure, implementation, integration, human review, correction, exception handling, controls, and ongoing operation against the value the organization can actually attribute to the investment.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Can the work support an AI investment case for the board?</h4><p>Yes. The briefing can clarify the claimed return, payback assumptions, material cost categories, labor implications, accountability, and key risks the board should understand before approving or expanding the investment.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>Can the analysis evaluate AI-related headcount or redeployment claims?</h4><p>The work can test whether the proposal distinguishes eliminated work from work relocated into review, correction, escalation, integration, or accountability. It does not provide workforce administration or legal advice.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>How is this different from vendor research?</h4><p>Lozen Advisory does not sell AI software or measure success by deployment. The analysis begins with the CFO decision, tests the underlying evidence, and identifies financial and governance exposure that adoption reporting may omit.</p></div>
    <div class="qa reveal"><h4>What does the CFO receive?</h4><p>A concise independent analysis of the investment question, the evidence supporting the claimed return, the costs and assumptions current reporting may be missing, and the questions finance and the board should resolve next.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<ConsultForm serviceHighlight="cfo market intelligence" selectedService="CFO Market Intelligence" />
</BaseLayout>
